# Everything in this repository is text and is stored and checked out with LF endings.
#
# Without this the repository drifts: the v0.2.0 import brought in 32 files with CRLF, a
# Windows checkout then rewrote the rest of the working tree to CRLF, and `git status` showed
# 54 modified files that differed from their committed versions by nothing but line endings.
# That is not merely untidy -- it hides real changes in the noise, and it makes patches
# generated on one machine fail to apply on the other.
#
# `eol=lf` applies on checkout regardless of a user's core.autocrlf, so this file is the fix
# rather than a per-clone setting that each person has to remember.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The shader sources are compiled at run time by the game's d3dx9; keep them LF too so the
# line numbers in a compiler error match the file as it is on disk.
*.hlsl text eol=lf

# Release archives are binary. `text=auto` already detects that, but saying so
# explicitly means no tool -- or careless one-liner -- can be talked into rewriting them.
*.zip binary
